                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\" xml:lang=\"en\"><p><b>Discharge diagnosis:</b> Displaced fracture of the right femoral neck, Garden IV (S72.0), treated with a cemented bipolar hemiarthroplasty on 10 November 2026. Postoperative anaemia, not transfused</p><ul><li>Femoral neck fracture, right (Garden IV), fall in Reykjavík</li></ul></div>"
            },
            "entry": [
              {
                "reference": "urn:uuid:a2e00005-0000-4000-8000-000000000013"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Hospital course",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "code": "8648-8",
                  "display": "Hospital course note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" lang=\"en\" xml:lang=\"en\"><p><b>Reason for transfer:</b> Return home to Sweden after surgery for a right femoral neck fracture; care continues at Vårdcentralen Kvarnängen and Sjöbacka kommun</p><p><b>Event abroad:</b> Fell on the stairs at his son&#x27;s home in Reykjavík on 9 November 2026: displaced right femoral neck fracture (Garden IV, S72.0)</p><p><b>Admitted:</b> 9 November 2026</p><p><b>Procedure:</b> Cemented bipolar hemiarthroplasty of the right hip, posterior approach, under spinal anaesthesia; clindamycin prophylaxis because of the penicillin allergy. Uncomplicated, 10 November 2026</p><p><b>Course:</b> Admitted through the emergency department on 9 November after a fall at his son&#x27;s home in Reykjavík. Apixaban paused; operated the next day under spinal anaesthesia, without complications. Mobilised with the physiotherapist from the first day after surgery, full weight bearing. Haemoglobin fell from 128 to 102 g/L. Blood glucose up to 14 mmol/L, managed with his own insulin glargine. Apixaban restarted on 12 November. Wound dry and healing. Fit to travel home on 20 November</p></div>"
            }
          },
